Nobody seems to have answered that (sorry if I overlooked it), hope you
haven't tried yet. It is safe when you do it right. You need to first
enchant your weapon to +5. A weapon enchanted above that has a chance of
being destroyed with the next scroll. However, at +5, a _blessed_ scroll
can add either one or two points. If you get the two, you end up at +7. If
you get only one, you end up at +6 and are now unsafe to read another
scroll until you remove one point (e.g. by engraving with an edged weapon).

